..Body
Whereas, The Community Foundation for Southeast Michigan administers the Ralph C. Wilson, Jr. Trails Maintenance Fund to support the repair, renovation, and maintenance of regional trail infrastructure and capital assets;

Whereas, The Community Foundation for Southeast Michigan has awarded a grant of $500,000.00 to the City of Ann Arbor to support the replacement of the South Barton Pedestrian Bridge over the Huron River on the Border to Border and Iron Belle Trails; 

Whereas, The South Barton Pedestrian Bridge is a key connection within the City’s non-motorized trail network and provides pedestrian and bicycle access across the Huron River within Barton Nature Area;

Whereas, The total project cost, including design and engineering, is currently estimated at approximately $5,000,000.00;

Whereas, The $500,000.00 grant will provide approximately 10% of the estimated total project cost; and

Whereas, Remaining project costs anticipated to be funded through a future Park Capital Improvement Bond;

RESOLVED, That City Council accepts $500,000.00 in grant funding from the Community Foundation for Southeast Michigan for the replacement of the South Barton Pedestrian Bridge;

RESOLVED, That City Council appropriates the $500,000.00 in grant funding to the South Barton Pedestrian Bridge replacement project budget;

RESOLVED, That all amounts herein are without regard to fiscal year;

RESOLVED, That City Council approves the attached grant agreement between the City of Ann Arbor and the Community Foundation for Southeast Michigan;  

RESOLVED, That the Mayor and City Clerk are authorized and directed to the sign the grant agreement after approval by the City Administrator and City Attorney; and

RESOLVED, That the City Administrator is authorized to take all appropriate actions to implement this resolution and the grant agreement, including execution of sub agreements, change orders, or related documents, and to make all determinations and exercise all authority delegated to the City under the grant agreement.
